From 91d35f4ec2c2919e974c90797c3b68ba975d168d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shyalya <shyalya@turtle-server.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:02:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Fix playerbot battleground queueing and make bots
 actually fight

Queueing:
- Bots queuing for a BG now go through the opcode handler directly instead of ai->QueuePacket() - bot sessions are never registered in sWorld.m_sessions, so World::UpdateSessions() never drained their recvQueue and the join packet silently vanished forever.
- Falls back to a server-accepted dummy battlemaster guid (1337) when no physical Battlemaster NPC is loaded nearby, instead of requiring one.
- WSG/AB matches now have a 20-minute hard cutoff (winner = whoever's ahead on points/flags) so bot-heavy matches that never cap objectives don't run forever.

Combat engagement (previously bots only ever fought back when a human player directly attacked them - never proactively, and never assisting each other):
- The +pvp strategy's "enemy player near" trigger was only wired into the combat engine, which an idle bot never entered on its own - now also registered for the non-combat engine and applied to both engines on BG entry.
- The underlying "enemy player targets" list was built exclusively from "attackers" (units already in an active threat relationship), so an idle enemy who hadn't attacked anyone was invisible to this whole detection chain. Now falls back to "possible targets" (a genuine proximity scan, no threat-table dependency) when in a battleground.
- AttackEnemyFlagCarrierAction::isUseful() checked the wrong unit's aura (a copy-paste bug from a neighboring function), requiring the *attacking* bot to already be a flag carrier itself instead of checking the *target* - bots chased flag carriers forever without ever attacking once they caught up.
